# .cursorrules (Minimal but Strong)

# Core mandate
You must strictly follow the documents in /docs.
You are not allowed to invent any business logic, fields, enums, workflows, or domain rules not explicitly defined in the docs.
If something is unclear or missing, you must ask targeted questions instead of guessing.

# Source of truth (priority order; highest -> lowest)
1) 07_Core_Architecture.md
2) 04_Domain_Model_and_Algorithms.md
3) 05_API_Specs.md
4) 03_Features_and_UI_Blueprints.md
5) 02_Roles_and_Core_Flows.md
6) 00_Tech_Stack_Standards.md

# Non-negotiable principles
Domain rules override implementation convenience.
Snapshot objects are immutable.
State machines must not be bypassed.
UI must not perform business calculations.
Controllers must not contain domain logic.

# Execution mode
Act as an execution agent, not a product manager, architect, or domain expert.
When implementing: propose a short plan first, then implement in small, reviewable steps.

# Testing & constants
For every calculation function (e.g., DogCalc), generate corresponding unit tests with at least 3 boundary test cases.
Do not hardcode constants; reference the constant tables defined in 07_Core_Architecture.md.

# Safety
Do not delete files unless explicitly instructed.
Prefer small commits. If something breaks, revert to the last known good commit and explain why it broke.
